Expected elements: missing

Finding #1 is a presence failure, so the rating is capped at 4: the replay telemetry — instructions executed, effects matched, `effectsMismatched: 0` — appears nowhere. The transaction pane runs Data, Block, Type, Age, Canonical, Finality, Cost, Executions, Decoded input, Selector, Raw, then clips mid-`RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` at y1075.

On my lens the theme is designed, not inverted: the code well is recessed below its pane in both themes (#ececeb under #ffffff here, #0d0d0d under #1b1b1b in dark) rather than mirrored, and the ladder #101010/#242424/#484848/#565656 over #ffffff/#f3f3f3/#dddddd/#ececeb holds.

**1.16:1 is withdrawn as a text ratio.** `"hydrationRounds": 6,` is not in this image. The `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` well is visible only from y1051 to y1074 and holds exactly one piece of ink: a 4x7px fragment at x1558-1561, y1067-1073, the top-left of the `{` of line 0. Its peak against its own row is 1.67:1 (#c4c4c4 on #fafafa, y1068). 1.16:1 reproduces only at y1072, on that glyph's antialiased tail (#ececec on #fdfdfd). At x1800 — the earlier report's stated sampling column — y1051-1074 is a pure #ececeb-to-#ffffff ramp with no glyph at any row, so the "descender" figure compared two backgrounds. Dark's same glyph peaks at 2.28:1, not 6.17:1: a 1.37x theme gap, not 5x.

Fixes: telemetry above the fold; move the code surface out of the masked subtree.

